<h2 id="agra">1. Agra: the Taj Mahal in a day</h2>
<p>The Yamuna Expressway makes Agra the easiest group day trip from Delhi. See the Taj Mahal at sunrise, explore Agra Fort, grab petha and Mughlai food, and be home by night. Add Mathura or Fatehpur Sikri if you have time. <em>Note: the Taj Mahal is closed on Fridays.</em> <a href="delhi-to-agra-tempo-on-rent.php">Book a Delhi to Agra tempo traveller →</a></p>

<h2 id="mathura">2. Mathura &amp; Vrindavan: a spiritual day out</h2>
<p>Perfect for families with elders. Visit Krishna Janmabhoomi, Banke Bihari Temple, Prem Mandir (beautifully lit at night) and ISKCON Vrindavan, all within a comfortable drive of Delhi. Holi and Janmashtami here are unforgettable, but very crowded.</p>

<h2 id="rishikesh">3. Rishikesh: adventure and aarti</h2>
<p>River rafting from Shivpuri, riverside camping, cafes around Laxman Jhula and the evening Ganga Aarti at Parmarth Niketan or Triveni Ghat. Rishikesh has something for every kind of group. Rafting usually pauses during the peak monsoon. <a href="delhi-to-rishikesh-tempo-on-rent.php">Delhi to Rishikesh tempo traveller →</a></p>

<h2 id="haridwar">4. Haridwar: Har Ki Pauri Ganga Aarti</h2>
<p>The evening aarti at Har Ki Pauri is one of India’s most moving sights. Take the ropeway to Mansa Devi and Chandi Devi temples, then continue to Rishikesh, just 25 km away, the next day. <a href="delhi-to-haridwar-tempo-on-rent.php">Delhi to Haridwar tempo traveller →</a></p>

<h2 id="jaipur">5. Jaipur: forts, palaces and bazaars</h2>
<p>Amer Fort, Hawa Mahal, City Palace, Nahargarh sunsets and shopping at Johari Bazaar: the Pink City packs a lot into a weekend. Stop at Neemrana on the way for a break. <a href="delhi-to-jaipur-tempo-on-rent.php">Delhi to Jaipur tempo traveller →</a></p>

<h2 id="chandigarh">6. Chandigarh &amp; Kasauli: city plus hills</h2>
<p>Spend a morning at the Rock Garden and Sukhna Lake, then drive up to Kasauli for colonial charm, pine walks and sunset at Monkey Point. It is a great mix for groups with different interests. <a href="delhi-to-chandigarh-tempo-on-rent.php">Delhi to Chandigarh tempo traveller →</a></p>

<h2 id="corbett">7. Jim Corbett: jungle safari weekend</h2>
<p>India’s oldest national park offers jeep safaris, riverside resorts and a chance to spot tigers, elephants and deer. Book safari zones well in advance, especially from November to June. Our <a href="wildlife-tempo-package.php">wildlife tempo traveller package</a> covers Corbett and more.</p>

<h2 id="mussoorie">8. Mussoorie: Queen of the Hills</h2>
<p>Mall Road walks, Kempty Falls, Gun Hill ropeway and cosy cafes on Camel’s Back Road. Mussoorie is the closest proper hill station for a Delhi group. Leave on Friday night to beat the weekend traffic. <a href="delhi-to-mussoorie-tempo-on-rent.php">Delhi to Mussoorie tempo traveller →</a></p>

<h2 id="nainital">9. Nainital: lakes of Kumaon</h2>
<p>Boat on Naini Lake, ride up to Snow View Point, and visit the quieter lakes of Bhimtal, Sattal and Naukuchiatal. For big groups, staying around Bhimtal avoids Nainital’s tight parking. <a href="delhi-to-nainital-tempo-on-rent.php">Delhi to Nainital tempo traveller →</a></p>

<h2 id="shimla">10. Shimla: the classic hill getaway</h2>
<p>The Ridge, Mall Road, Christ Church, Jakhoo Temple and a day trip to Kufri and Chail. Shimla is a timeless choice for families. Winter brings snowfall around Kufri and Narkanda. <a href="delhi-to-shimla-tempo-on-rent.php">Delhi to Shimla tempo traveller →</a></p>

<h2 id="planning-tips">Tips for a smooth weekend road trip</h2>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Leave early.</strong> Crossing Delhi before 6 am saves hours.</li>
    <li><strong>Pick the right vehicle size</strong> for your group and luggage. Our <a href="12-16-20-seater-tempo-traveller-which-to-choose.php">seater comparison</a> helps.</li>
    <li><strong>Book hotels with parking</strong> for a tempo traveller, especially in hill towns.</li>
    <li><strong>Share one pick-up plan.</strong> We can collect everyone from multiple points in Delhi NCR.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the price in advance.</strong> See our <a href="tempo-traveller-on-rent-in-delhi-price-guide.php">tempo traveller price guide</a> to budget accurately.</li>
</ol>
